; Regression test for issue #3327: a total of several columns is revalued
; only up to the report's terminus, as before.
;
; The salary is dated after --now, when ABC is worth $25 rather than the
; $20 it is worth at the terminus.  A balance report values its accounts at
; the terminus, so it revalues its running total back to the terminus and
; books the $100 gain over the $10 cost.  The market value and cost pairs
; of --gain, and the totals that cleared keeps, gather no gain from cost
; basis, so revaluing them back would book only the $50 fall from $25.

2024/01/01 * Buy
    Assets:Broker    10 ABC @ $10
    Assets:Cash

P 2024/02/01 ABC $20
P 2024/03/15 ABC $25

2024/04/01 * Salary
    Assets:Cash    $50
    Income:Salary

test bal -V --unrealized --now 2024/03/01
                $150  Assets
                $200    Broker
                $-50    Cash
               $-100  Equity:Unrealized Gains
                $-50  Income:Salary
--------------------
                   0
end test

test bal -G --unrealized --now 2024/03/01
                $100  Assets:Broker
end test

test cleared -V --unrealized --now 2024/03/01
            $150                $150                 Assets
            $200                $200    24-Jan-01      Broker
            $-50                $-50    24-Apr-01      Cash
            $-50                $-50    24-Apr-01    Income:Salary
----------------  ------------------    ---------
            $100                $100             
end test
